 "script": [
  {
   "id": "hook",
   "text": "Eighty-one million Thanksgiving travelers. And a powerful storm is heading for the East Coast."
  },
  {
   "id": "f1",
   "text": "Charleston first. Forecasters expect its harbor gauge to pass eight feet at Wednesday morning's high tide, CNN reports. NOAA says that level floods numerous downtown roads. Moderate to major coastal flooding is possible from Georgia to Long Island, The Weather Channel says."
  },
  {
   "id": "f2",
   "text": "Then the Northeast. The National Weather Service has a high wind watch for New York City and Philadelphia on Thanksgiving Day, ABC News reports, with gusts up to sixty miles an hour. Forecasters also expect one to two inches of rain."
  },
  {
   "id": "f3",
   "text": "That puts the hundredth Macy's parade at risk. Under city rules, the giant balloons stay down if gusts top thirty-four miles an hour, CNN reports. Officials will decide on the day. AAA expects eighty-one and a half million travelers this week."
  },
  {
   "id": "cta",
   "text": "Will the giant balloons fly on Thanksgiving morning? Yes or no?"
  }
 ],
