  "title": "East Coast Storm Threatens Thanksgiving and Macy's Parade #shorts",
  "description": "A powerful coastal storm is expected to move up the U.S. East Coast over Thanksgiving. Forecasters cited by CNN expect Charleston's harbor gauge to pass 8 feet on Wednesday morning, and The Weather Channel says moderate to major coastal flooding is possible from Georgia to Long Island. The National Weather Service has a high wind watch for New York City and Philadelphia on Thanksgiving Day with gusts up to 60 mph, while city rules ground the Macy's parade balloons if gusts top 34 mph. AAA expects 81.5 million Thanksgiving travelers.\n\nSources: CNN, ABC News, The Weather Channel, Fox Weather, AAA (based on search-result excerpts). Flood zone and storm path on the map are approximate and illustrative.\n\n#climate #weather #thanksgiving #noreaster #coastalflooding",
